sections.body:
```
GET /search?... → [room_offer]
POST /holds → { hold_token, expires_at }
POST /bookings (Idem-Key) → { booking_id, status, confirmation_code }
POST /bookings/:id/cancel → { status: "cancelled" }
GET /bookings/:id → booking + payment status
```

```sql
TABLE bookings ( booking_id UUID PRIMARY KEY, idempotency_key TEXT UNIQUE, user_id UUID, hotel_id UUID, room_type_id UUID, check_in DATE, check_out DATE, status ENUM('pending','confirmed','cancelled','failed'), charge_id TEXT, created_at TIMESTAMPTZ, updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ
);
TABLE room_inventory (...); -- see Inventory Service
TABLE outbox (event_type, payload, created_at, delivered_at);
```

```sql
BEGIN; -- guard against oversell; 0 rows = sold out UPDATE room_inventory SET booked_rooms = booked_rooms + 1 WHERE hotel_id =? AND room_type_id =? AND date =? AND booked_rooms < total_rooms; INSERT INTO bookings (booking_id, idempotency_key,...) VALUES (...); INSERT INTO outbox (event_type, payload) VALUES ('booking_confirmed',...);
COMMIT;
```
Write isolation: REPEATABLE READ (MySQL default) or SERIALIZABLE — the guarded UPDATE is safe under both.

